  "query_preview": "(This evening through Thursday)...\nIssued at 202 PM EST Thu Nov 5 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Friday...\n\nClouds covered the northwest half or so of the forecast area this \nafternoon, with mostly clear skies southeast. Under clouds, readings \nwere in the 50s, with 60s in sunshine.\n\nAs an upper trough and surface cold front approach the area, the \nclouds will gradually overspread all of central Indiana into this \nevening. Best forcing with this system will be north of central \nIndiana, closer to the heart of the upper system. Moisture isn't \ngreat, but the system may be able to squeeze out some light rain as \nit moves through.\n\nWill generally cap PoPs at the chance category tonight, with the \nhighest PoPs north. \n\nOn Friday, colder air flowing in from the northwest will generate \nsome lake enhanced showers across northern Indiana. Some of these \nmay sneak into the far northern forecast area, so will have some low \nPoPs there. Otherwise, cold advection should aid in keeping skies \nmostly cloudy. \n\nLows tonight will be in the 40s, with highs on Friday in the lower \n50s thanks to cold advection and lack of significant sunshine.\n\nSaturday onward...\n\nCentral Indiana will remain in northwest flow aloft, with upper \nsystems moving well to the north or south of the area. Moisture will \nbe kept south of the area, so any weak forcing that does move into \nthe area will have nothing to work with. Will continue a dry \nforecast into mid-week next week. \n\nTemperatures will start out cool in the 50s this weekend, but then \nmoderate into the 60s for early next week.",
